      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "P2P tunnels are channel teleporters: one tunnel packs up to 32 channels into a single channel and delivers them at its twin. Each tunnel itself needs one free channel; tunnels cannot nest; a regular cable carries 4 tunnel links, a dense one 16.\n\nThe standard trick: dedicate a second controller as a transport net, feed everything into P2P at one end, fan out at the other. Base-wide channel problems end here.\n\nThe legacy line paid this quest out in memory cards, and so do we: an advanced memory card from BetterP2P links and re-links tunnels in bulk, plus a stock of tunnels and the interface-parallelizer parts the old-timers rave about.",
